The Midgaard River slides beneath a broad stone bridge and through a low arch in the
western city wall. Water-dark masonry rises on either side, its lower courses slick
with moss and riverweed. Above, the muted rumble of carts and boots crosses the bridge
while the current carries leaves and driftwood eastward through the city.
