wall masonry stones mortar bridge~
Massive gray stones form the riverward wall and the bridge abutment above it. The
blocks are fitted tightly and sealed with pale mortar, with centuries of damp staining
the lowest courses. The work is heavy, practical, and clearly meant to withstand both
floodwater and siege.
