A break in the northern embankment has been reinforced with broad stone steps leading
up from the river toward the city levee. Iron rings are set into the masonry for tying
small workboats, and worn grooves show where ropes and cargo have been hauled over the
years. East and west, the Midgaard River continues through its walled channel.
