bars iron gate grate river eastern wall~
Thick iron bars have been driven deep into the stonework above and below the waterline.
Their surfaces are scarred by rust, flood debris, and years of maintenance, but the
grate remains formidable. Through the gaps, the river can be seen continuing into
darkness beneath the eastern hills.
